1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,460
Zero tax on a 10 lakh salary,

2
00:00:02,460 --> 00:00:04,920
and still Papa was getting her to buy policies.

3
00:00:04,920 --> 00:00:08,084
This story is about my sister. Her first big job,

4
00:00:08,084 --> 00:00:11,950
her first big salary. And in the very first week, an email came from HR.

5
00:00:11,950 --> 00:00:14,410
The question was: old regime or new?

6
00:00:14,410 --> 00:00:18,193
In the evening, the whole family was reading this email at the dining table.

7
00:00:18,193 --> 00:00:20,715
My sister opened her laptop, Mummy brought tea.

8
00:00:20,715 --> 00:00:24,183
Papa put on his glasses and said straight away: Take the old regime, beta,

9
00:00:24,183 --> 00:00:27,020
we've always been in that. That one is safe.

10
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:28,816
Papa's reasoning was simple.

11
00:00:28,816 --> 00:00:32,409
In the old regime there are ways to save tax. Take a policy,

12
00:00:32,409 --> 00:00:36,002
open a PPF, lock in an FD, and your tax goes down.

13
00:00:36,002 --> 00:00:39,236
For him, saving tax meant buying something or other.

14
00:00:39,236 --> 00:00:42,110
Every March, for years, this is what had happened.

15
00:00:42,110 --> 00:00:45,679
My brother was on the sofa in a hoodie, phone in hand. He said, Papa,

16
00:00:45,679 --> 00:00:48,924
take the new regime, everyone on the internet is saying that.

17
00:00:48,924 --> 00:00:52,169
Papa asked, why? My brother had no answer.

18
00:00:52,169 --> 00:00:54,440
All he remembered was a reel he saw in the morning.

19
00:00:54,440 --> 00:00:57,770
And this is the real problem. On one side there's habit,

20
00:00:57,770 --> 00:00:58,880
on the other side, a reel.

21
00:00:58,880 --> 00:01:02,210
In the middle is the person whose salary is getting cut.

22
00:01:02,210 --> 00:01:06,280
Nobody shows them the actual calculation. So today we'll do the calculation,

23
00:01:06,280 --> 00:01:08,130
just like at the dining table, straight and simple.

24
00:01:08,130 --> 00:01:09,855
Today's questions are these.

25
00:01:09,855 --> 00:01:12,270
Is the new regime cheaper for everyone?

26
00:01:12,270 --> 00:01:16,065
Is 80C still useful, or is it just habit?

27
00:01:16,065 --> 00:01:18,480
And HRA, meaning the tax exemption on rent,

28
00:01:18,480 --> 00:01:20,550
when does it really help?

29
00:01:20,550 --> 00:01:22,620
The answer comes from this same family's story.

30
00:01:22,620 --> 00:01:26,245
First, let's clear one thing up. Regime means the tax rulebook.

31
00:01:26,245 --> 00:01:29,211
The government has put both rulebooks in front of you.

32
00:01:29,211 --> 00:01:32,836
In the old one, rates are higher, but there are lots of exemptions. In the new one, rates are lower,

33
00:01:32,836 --> 00:01:34,813
but exemptions are very few. If you say nothing,

34
00:01:34,813 --> 00:01:36,790
the new one applies automatically.

35
00:01:36,790 --> 00:01:40,321
That night I opened my sister's salary slip with her.

36
00:01:40,321 --> 00:01:44,205
At the top is gross salary, meaning your full earnings before any cuts.

37
00:01:44,205 --> 00:01:46,323
Below that, PF and one line, TDS.

38
00:01:46,323 --> 00:01:50,560
TDS means the company deducts your tax in advance every month.

39
00:01:50,560 --> 00:01:54,909
In the new regime, salaried people get a straight 75,000 exemption.

40
00:01:54,909 --> 00:01:58,896
This is called the standard deduction. No policy, no receipt,

41
00:01:58,896 --> 00:02:01,795
No proof needed. You just have to be in a job,

42
00:02:01,795 --> 00:02:03,970
and this much portion is outside tax.

43
00:02:03,970 --> 00:02:07,687
Meaning this portion is taken out of your salary first.

44
00:02:07,687 --> 00:02:10,661
What remains is called taxable income.

45
00:02:10,661 --> 00:02:15,121
Taxable income means the earnings on which tax is actually charged.

46
00:02:15,121 --> 00:02:16,980
Now comes the real twist.

47
00:02:16,980 --> 00:02:21,485
Under the new regime, there is zero tax on taxable income up to 12 lakh.

48
00:02:21,485 --> 00:02:24,258
This happens because of the Section 87A rebate.

49
00:02:24,258 --> 00:02:26,337
Rebate means tax does get calculated,

50
00:02:26,337 --> 00:02:29,110
but the government waives it completely.

51
00:02:29,110 --> 00:02:32,999
My sister's taxable income was well below this limit.

52
00:02:32,999 --> 00:02:36,887
So under the new regime, her income tax is zero. No policy,

53
00:02:36,887 --> 00:02:39,220
no lock-in, no March rush.

54
00:02:39,220 --> 00:02:42,720
Papa took off his glasses and looked at the screen again.

55
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:45,843
For salaried people, this benefit becomes even bigger.

56
00:02:45,843 --> 00:02:48,653
First a 75,000 deduction, then a rebate up to 12 lakh.

57
00:02:48,653 --> 00:02:52,712
Together, the two keep a pretty decent salary out of tax.

58
00:02:52,712 --> 00:02:55,210
Many people never even add this up.

59
00:02:55,210 --> 00:02:58,206
So is the new regime cheaper for everyone? No,

60
00:02:58,206 --> 00:03:01,202
not for everyone. For those whose salary is in this range,

61
00:03:01,202 --> 00:03:04,198
often yes. But for those who earn more,

62
00:03:04,198 --> 00:03:07,860
and have a lot of deductions, the story may be different.

63
00:03:07,860 --> 00:03:09,667
One more thing to keep in mind.

64
00:03:09,667 --> 00:03:12,557
This rebate is for normal income like salary.

65
00:03:12,557 --> 00:03:16,532
Profit made by selling shares, that is, capital gains, has separate rules.

66
00:03:16,532 --> 00:03:18,699
If you also do trading,

67
00:03:18,699 --> 00:03:21,590
do get your full accounts checked by a CA.

68
00:03:21,590 --> 00:03:23,854
Now Papa's question. Beta,

69
00:03:23,854 --> 00:03:28,836
so are my LIC and PPF all useless? This is important to understand here.

70
00:03:28,836 --> 00:03:32,007
80C is that section of the old regime

71
00:03:32,007 --> 00:03:35,177
where you get a deduction on certain investments.

72
00:03:35,177 --> 00:03:38,800
Under the new regime, you don't get this deduction at all.

73
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:43,115
In the old regime, the 80C limit is 1.5 lakh. PPF, EPF,

74
00:03:43,115 --> 00:03:47,038
life insurance premium, tax saving fund, all together up to this much.

75
00:03:47,038 --> 00:03:50,176
This amount is subtracted from your taxable income.

76
00:03:50,176 --> 00:03:52,530
It sounds very big.

77
00:03:52,530 --> 00:03:55,032
But there is one thing Papa never counted.

78
00:03:55,032 --> 00:03:58,160
EPF is already being deducted from my sister's salary.

79
00:03:58,160 --> 00:03:59,411
EPF means provident fund,

80
00:03:59,411 --> 00:04:01,914
which you and the company both put in every month.

81
00:04:01,914 --> 00:04:03,790
That also counts under 80C.

82
00:04:03,790 --> 00:04:05,980
Part of the limit is already used up.

83
00:04:05,980 --> 00:04:09,222
Now imagine the sister listened to Papa.

84
00:04:09,222 --> 00:04:13,186
She took the old regime, and in March she bought an insurance policy.

85
00:04:13,186 --> 00:04:16,788
Paying premiums for years, a lock-in, and no idea what the returns will be.

86
00:04:16,788 --> 00:04:18,950
Only because she wanted to save tax.

87
00:04:18,950 --> 00:04:22,238
But under the new regime, her tax was already zero.

88
00:04:22,238 --> 00:04:24,869
The tax she bought the policy to save,

89
00:04:24,869 --> 00:04:26,513
that tax didn't even exist.

90
00:04:26,513 --> 00:04:28,814
She got no tax benefit from the policy.

91
00:04:28,814 --> 00:04:31,445
Her money just got locked up for years.

92
00:04:31,445 --> 00:04:32,760
This is the trap.

93
00:04:32,760 --> 00:04:35,709
This doesn't mean PPF is bad.

94
00:04:35,709 --> 00:04:39,028
PPF currently gives about 7.1 percent interest per year.

95
00:04:39,028 --> 00:04:42,346
People like it for long-term savings.

96
00:04:42,346 --> 00:04:44,927
Just open a PPF for savings,

97
00:04:44,927 --> 00:04:46,770
not out of fear of tax.

98
00:04:46,770 --> 00:04:49,568
So is 80C useful now or not?

99
00:04:49,568 --> 00:04:52,716
If you're in the old regime, yes, very useful.

100
00:04:52,716 --> 00:04:56,213
If you're in the new regime, not at all for tax.

101
00:04:56,213 --> 00:05:00,060
First choose your regime, then think about whether you even need 80C.

102
00:05:00,060 --> 00:05:02,464
Papa stayed quiet for a bit and said,

103
00:05:02,464 --> 00:05:05,898
So I did it wrong all these years? I said, no Papa.

104
00:05:05,898 --> 00:05:08,646
In your time, there was no new regime.

105
00:05:08,646 --> 00:05:11,393
Back then, that was the right thing. Only the rules changed,

106
00:05:11,393 --> 00:05:13,110
and we didn't change our habits.

107
00:05:13,110 --> 00:05:14,732
Now the other side of the story.

108
00:05:14,732 --> 00:05:17,328
The new regime doesn't win for everyone.

109
00:05:17,328 --> 00:05:19,275
Look at the sister's colleague.

110
00:05:19,275 --> 00:05:21,871
She lives in a big city on rent.

111
00:05:21,871 --> 00:05:25,440
She pays for her Mummy-Papa's health insurance. And her salary is quite high.

112
00:05:25,440 --> 00:05:28,050
First understand HRA. HRA means House Rent Allowance,

113
00:05:28,050 --> 00:05:30,334
which the company gives for rent.

114
00:05:30,334 --> 00:05:34,249
Under the old regime, a big part of it can be tax-free,

115
00:05:34,249 --> 00:05:36,533
if you really pay rent.

116
00:05:36,533 --> 00:05:38,490
Under the new regime, there's no such exemption.

117
00:05:38,490 --> 00:05:41,782
So keep your rent receipts and your landlord's details safe.

118
00:05:41,782 --> 00:05:44,415
And for people who live in their own house,

119
00:05:44,415 --> 00:05:47,048
there's no question of an HRA exemption.

120
00:05:47,048 --> 00:05:50,340
There, HRA just becomes the taxable part of the salary.

121
00:05:50,340 --> 00:05:51,268
Now, home loan.

122
00:05:51,268 --> 00:05:55,597
Under the old regime, you also get a deduction on the interest on your home loan.

123
00:05:55,597 --> 00:05:58,999
Interest means the part of the loan that is the bank's profit.

124
00:05:58,999 --> 00:06:02,710
Under the old regime, the health insurance premium is also subtracted from your income.

125
00:06:02,710 --> 00:06:07,033
The colleague added it all up. Rent deduction, 80C, health insurance.

126
00:06:07,033 --> 00:06:12,220
Deductions means the expenses that are subtracted from taxable income.

127
00:06:12,220 --> 00:06:16,111
His deductions have become very big. The bigger the deductions,

128
00:06:16,111 --> 00:06:17,840
the more attractive the old regime.

129
00:06:17,840 --> 00:06:22,884
His salary is so high that under the new regime it goes up to the higher slabs.

130
00:06:22,884 --> 00:06:26,486
Slab means chunks of income, with a different rate on each chunk.

131
00:06:26,486 --> 00:06:29,729
The highest slab in the new regime is 30 percent,

132
00:06:29,729 --> 00:06:31,170
above 24 lakh.

133
00:06:31,170 --> 00:06:34,493
On such an income, the zero-tax rebate doesn't work.

134
00:06:34,493 --> 00:06:37,483
Now every rupee of deduction saves real money.

135
00:06:37,483 --> 00:06:41,470
That's why the big deductions of the old regime can really make a difference.

136
00:06:41,470 --> 00:06:44,460
In his case, the old regime can even win.

137
00:06:44,460 --> 00:06:47,576
So the formula is simple. Work out the tax under both regimes,

138
00:06:47,576 --> 00:06:49,306
and choose whichever comes out lower.

139
00:06:49,306 --> 00:06:51,730
There is a calculator on the Income Tax website.

140
00:06:51,730 --> 00:06:55,538
You can see both calculations side by side there. Don't guess,

141
00:06:55,538 --> 00:06:56,230
look at the numbers.

142
00:06:56,230 --> 00:06:59,018
Now, the mistake most people make.

143
00:06:59,018 --> 00:07:01,806
They choose a regime out of habit, not by calculation.

144
00:07:01,806 --> 00:07:04,594
Some stick to the old one like Papa.

145
00:07:04,594 --> 00:07:07,691
Some switch to the new one after watching a reel, like Bhai.

146
00:07:07,691 --> 00:07:09,240
In both, the calculation is missing.

147
00:07:09,240 --> 00:07:12,215
The second mistake, the March rush. Nothing all year,

148
00:07:12,215 --> 00:07:14,528
and then in the last week, any policy at all.

149
00:07:14,528 --> 00:07:16,181
Just to save tax.

150
00:07:16,181 --> 00:07:19,816
Buy a product for what it does, not for tax.

151
00:07:19,816 --> 00:07:22,130
A deduction can be a bonus, not the reason.

152
00:07:22,130 --> 00:07:23,821
Now, how do you switch?

153
00:07:23,821 --> 00:07:27,880
If you're salaried, you have to tell HR your regime at the start of the year.

154
00:07:27,880 --> 00:07:30,586
TDS is cut every month accordingly.

155
00:07:30,586 --> 00:07:34,307
If you don't tell them anything, the company assumes the new regime,

156
00:07:34,307 --> 00:07:35,660
because that is the default.

157
00:07:35,660 --> 00:07:37,003
Here's the good news.

158
00:07:37,003 --> 00:07:40,695
Salaried people can also change their regime when filing the return.

159
00:07:40,695 --> 00:07:41,702
Return means ITR,

160
00:07:41,702 --> 00:07:45,059
the complete account given to the government at the end of the year.

161
00:07:45,059 --> 00:07:46,738
Told HR the wrong thing,

162
00:07:46,738 --> 00:07:50,430
even then the decision can be changed in the return, within the deadline.

163
00:07:50,430 --> 00:07:52,984
Just keep this in mind. For those who have business income,

164
00:07:52,984 --> 00:07:54,899
switching is not that easy.

165
00:07:54,899 --> 00:07:57,772
They have very few chances to come back.

166
00:07:57,772 --> 00:07:59,687
If you have a shop or a practice,

167
00:07:59,687 --> 00:08:02,560
definitely ask someone who knows before changing regime.

168
00:08:02,560 --> 00:08:06,055
That night, my sister replied to HR: new regime.

169
00:08:06,055 --> 00:08:08,152
Dad looked at the calculation and said yes.

170
00:08:08,152 --> 00:08:10,948
The policy form went back into the drawer.

171
00:08:10,948 --> 00:08:13,744
PPF will still open, but for savings.

172
00:08:13,744 --> 00:08:16,890
This is not investment advice. Do your own calculation.

173
00:08:16,890 --> 00:08:20,681
So, your question. Which regime are you in right now,

174
00:08:20,681 --> 00:08:24,472
old or new? Just write old or new in the comments.

175
00:08:24,472 --> 00:08:28,264
And if you don't know at all, then look at your salary slip.

176
00:08:28,264 --> 00:08:29,780
That is the first step.

177
00:08:29,780 --> 00:08:34,105
Next time, the question that comes up in every home.

178
00:08:34,105 --> 00:08:38,430
When is tax charged on selling shares, and when not?

179
00:08:38,430 --> 00:08:43,188
The whole story of capital gains, at this very dining table. Till then,

180
00:08:43,188 --> 00:08:45,350
learn to do your own calculation.
